## Generic-class lib-decl `.new` dispatch.
##
## Regression probe: a `def self.new as "<c-symbol>"(...)` lib decl on
## a GENERIC class (`Mutex[T]`, `SharedSync[T]`, `AtomicI64`, …) must
## route directly to the C symbol — not synthesise a phantom
## `Class_init(self, ...)` callee. Before the v1-missing-features
## 2026-05-20 fix, `Mutex.new(7)` produced an undefined symbol
## `_Mutex_init` linker error because the `is_collection_ctor` fast
## path in `mir/lower/expr/method_call.rs` only recognised a
## hardcoded list of legacy builtin classes (Vec / Hash / Set / File
## / Duration / Instant / etc.) and fell through to the
## `Class_init` synthesis for any other class — silently ignoring
## the lib-decl FFI alias for generic classes.
##
## The fix adds a generic `ffi_alias_map.contains_key("Class_new")`
## check at the start of the fast path so any class with a registered
## `def self.NAME as "..."` lib decl dispatches directly to its FFI
## symbol with no `self` prepended.

def main
  let m = Mutex.new(7)
  if m == 0
    puts "null"
  else
    puts "ok"
  end
end
